  data: {
    LLM: 'Players take turns playing a card to the discard pile that matches the previous card in rank OR suit. If unable to play, draw one card from the stock. If the drawn card is playable, it may be played immediately.',
    Player: 'Players take turns playing a card to the discard pile that matches the previous card in rank OR suit. If unable to play, draw one card from the stock. If the drawn card is playable, it may be played immediately.',
    objective: 'The object is to be the first player to have no cards left in your hand; the first to empty their hand wins the round.',
    gameplay: 'Players take turns playing a card to the discard pile that matches the previous card in rank OR suit. If unable to play, draw one card from the stock. If the drawn card is playable, it may be played immediately.',
    keyRules: [
      'Two (2): Next player draws 2 cards and loses their turn. Multiple 2s can be stacked (e.g., two 2s = draw 4).',
      'Three (3): May be played on any card and allows the player to play another card immediately (stacking).',
      "Four (4): Causes a 'melee'â€”the next player must play a 5 of the same suit if possible, then 6, etc. If the sequence stops, the current target draws cards equal to the last played rank.",
      'Eight (8): Wild card. Can be played on any card. Player announces a new suit that must be followed.',
      "Jack (J): Skip the next player's turn.",
      'Ace (A): Reverse direction of play. In 2-player games, acts as a Skip.',
      'Joker: Next player draws 5 cards (or 6, by agreement) and loses their turn. Cannot be stacked in most rules.',
      "Last Card Rule: When a player has exactly one card left, they MUST say 'Last One' (or 'Last Card'). If another player catches them not saying it before the next card is played, the offender must draw a penalty card (usually 1 or 2).",
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
